<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barolong</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rolong, Barolong people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Barolong are a Tswana-speaking people of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, among the oldest Tswana groups, traditionally settled in the southern Kalahari margins and the Molopo valley. After the death of the 18th-century chief Tau they split into branches, including the Ratlou, Tshidi, Seleka and Rapulana. Their descendants live today in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s North West and Free State provinces, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahikeng">Mahikeng</a> and Thaba Nchu, and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>.</p></div>
